{{also|Tauschen|täuschen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|tiuschen}}, which is derived from {{m|gmh|tūschen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈtaʊ̯ʃən/|[ˈtʰaʊ̯ʃn̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-tauschen.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{audio|de|De-tauschen.ogg}}
* {{hyph|de|tau|schen}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|''[''{{m|de|gegen|tr=for}}'']''}} to [[trade]], to [[exchange]], to [[swap]], to [[barter]] (items,  goods, etc.)
#: {{ux|de|Er '''tauschte''' die Büroklammer gegen einen Stift.|He '''exchanged''' the paper clip for a pen.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|figurative}} to do something mutually; to swap circumstances
#: {{uxi|de|die Plätze '''tauschen'''|to '''trade''' places}}
#: {{uxi|de|Küsse '''tauschen'''|to '''share''' a kiss}}
#: {{uxi|de|Grüße '''tauschen'''|to '''trade''' greetings}}

